# crack_baseline_v1 (2026-09-29): ONE parameter set for both 25 and 45 degC.
# Runs on the high_temp_45C fork (cell064_degradation_fit_45C.py) via
# crack_growth_sweep.py; everything not listed = the fork's own defaults
# (incl. SOLVENT_MULT=5, SI_ESEI=GR_ESEI=38000, SI_CRIT_STRESS=6e6,
# SI_LAM_EAC=40000, SI_LAM_ISO_EXPONENT=15, WIDTH=3e-4, Si-only aging deformations).
# Only the operating temperature differs between conditions:
#   25 degC: C64_T_AMBIENT_K=298.15   45 degC: C64_T_AMBIENT_K=318.15
# SI_CRACK_EAC / SI_LAM_EAC are exactly inert at 298.15 K (Arrhenius factor = 1).
C64_SI_CRACK_MULT=1.3e3
C64_SI_TAU_LAM_ISO=4e8
C64_SI_REDIRECT_LAM_YIELD=0.30
C64_GR_REDIRECT_TO_LAM=1
C64_GR_REDIRECT_LAM_YIELD=0.016
C64_GR_LAM_ISO_EXPONENT=10
C64_F0=0.7
C64_SI_CRACK_EAC=70000
